From: sneid1 <sneid1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 16:39:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] UYA: static recompilation of the EE code (recgen_iso.py rc3,
 rec table keyed on level_current)

tools/recgen_iso.py reads UYA's code from the disc (boot payload core, the boot program's front end as pseudo-level 100, frontbin as 101,
any level 1..55 from the level table) over bounds given with --bounds, leaves host-stubbed functions to the interpreter, and writes
r3* crates plus an ee-game-rc3 facade without the rc1-aot feature. ee-oracle: rec table range to 0x700000, front-end pseudo-levels
from 100, level_key = level_current (0x1d545c), table rebuild backstop at vblank, n_skip counter for the run report.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
